==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/swɒt/}}, /swŏt/
* {{audio|en|en-us-swat.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɒt}}

===Etymology 1===

====Verb====
{{en-verb|swatt}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[beat off]], as insects; to [[bat]], [[strike]], or [[hit]].
#: ''He '''swatted''' the mosquito that was buzzing around in his bedroom.''
#: ''The cat '''swatted''' at the feather.''
#* '''2017,''' {{w|Jennifer S. Holland}}, ''For These Monkeys, It’s a Fight for Survival.'', National Geographic (March 2017)[http://www.nationalgeographic.com/magazine/2017/03/macaques-monkeys-indonesia-endangered-pet-trade/]
#*: During my first day in the woods, Raoul, the big alpha male of Rambo II, opened wide to show me his dagger-sharp canines, then sauntered by and '''swatted''' my calf with a stick—letting me know my place in the social order. (Low.)

