===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*swait-}}, from {{der|ang|ine-pro|*swoyd-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*sweyd-}}. Cognate with {{cog|osx|swêt}}, {{cog|goh|sweiz}}, {{cog|non|sveiti||sweat, blood}}. The Indo-European root also gave {{cog|la|sudor}}, Sanskrit {{cog|sa|स्वेद}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|ang|/swɑːt/}}

===Noun===
{{ang-noun|m|g2=n|head=swāt}}

# [[sweat]]
# used of other moisture that comes from the body, especially [[blood]]

====Declension====
{{ang-decl-noun-a-m|swāt|num=sg}}

